  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Nigeria Programme for Country Partnership</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overarching aim is to convert the ongoing Nigeria Country Programme (CP) into Programme for Country Partnership (PCP) as a basis for providing technical cooperation and support for enhancing Nigeria#s economic diversification agenda as enshrined in the National Development Plan (NDP), 2021-2025. The technical support will be geared towards removal of binding constraints to manufacturing production and promote inclusive and sustainable industrial development thereby spurring economic structural transformation for prosperity and employment generation and poverty reduction through utilization of the country#s abundant human, material and other resources. The technical cooperation assistance which is aimed at promoting and developing green industries will take different forms including support for policy formulation/reviews and reforms, human and institutional capacity development as well as strengthening the capacity of enterprises in some manufacturing subsectors, industrial infrastructures development including renewable energy to enhance optimal manufacturing production and industrial competitiveness, build trust for trade and environmental management with particular emphasis on circular economy.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Regular Programme Of Technical Cooperati</narrative>
